On Solaris, uname can return any non-negative value on success;
on other platforms, it seems to be just zero.

Since -1 seems to be the error indicating return value everywhere,
this patch might be acceptable upstream.

This was reported upstream:
https://lore.kernel.org/git/SJ0PR10MB5785807828F81EAC8CA165E78A702@SJ0PR10MB5785.namprd10.prod.outlook.com/

--- git-2.56.0/version.c
+++ git-2.56.0/version.c
@@ -83,7 +83,7 @@ int get_uname_info(struct strbuf *buf, u
 {
 	struct utsname uname_info;
 
-	if (uname(&uname_info)) {
+	if (uname(&uname_info) < 0) {
 		strbuf_addf(buf, _("uname() failed with error '%s' (%d)\n"),
 			    strerror(errno),
 			    errno);
